1978
00:38:53,940 --> 00:38:58,100
Let not the one who eats despise the one who abstains.

1979
00:38:58,100 --> 00:39:04,280
Let not the one who abstains pass judgment on the one who eats, for God has welcomed him.

1980
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:09,000
He says, the temptation for the strong is to hate the weak.

1981
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:15,140
You rule followers, you black and white list makers, you guys are just annoying us.

1982
00:39:15,140 --> 00:39:17,540
You're making everything harder than it has to be.

1983
00:39:17,540 --> 00:39:19,860
Leave us alone and let us live in the gray.

1984
00:39:19,860 --> 00:39:22,320
You guys go sit at your own table in the black and white.

1985
00:39:22,320 --> 00:39:23,900
You guys are so frustrated.

1986
00:39:23,940 --> 00:39:31,000
The black and white are like, you guys don't obey anything God tells you to obey.

1987
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:33,540
You don't care about any of the rules or any of the regulations.

1988
00:39:33,540 --> 00:39:34,860
You make up your own stuff.

1989
00:39:34,860 --> 00:39:36,520
You do whatever you want to do, right?

1990
00:39:36,520 --> 00:39:38,620
Hatred towards the weak.

1991
00:39:38,620 --> 00:39:42,040
Judgmental towards the strong.

1992
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:45,760
How accurate is Paul's diagnosis of the human heart?

1993
00:39:48,220 --> 00:39:49,820
The strong will despise the weak.

1994
00:39:49,820 --> 00:39:51,500
The weak will become judgmental of the strong.

1995
00:39:51,500 --> 00:39:53,640
And both responses break the heart of God.

1996
00:39:53,640 --> 00:40:00,540
Paul's response to both is, the Lord will uphold your brother and your sister.

1997
00:40:02,380 --> 00:40:03,260
I love this.

1998
00:40:03,260 --> 00:40:04,800
Listen to this at the end of verse four.

1999
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:08,580
Who are we to pass judgment on the servant of another?

2000
00:40:08,580 --> 00:40:12,320
It is before his own master that he stands or falls.

2001
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:19,000
And he will be upheld for the Lord is able to make him stand.

2002
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:21,460
See, we justify these disagreements.

2003
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:24,640
We justify this disunity because we say it's for their own good.

2004
00:40:24,900 --> 00:40:26,500
We're trying to make sure they don't fall.

2005
00:40:26,500 --> 00:40:28,000
They're going to fall into sin.

2006
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:29,320
They're going to fall into religion.

2007
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:30,120
They're going to fall.

2008
00:40:30,120 --> 00:40:30,660
They're going to fall.

2009
00:40:30,660 --> 00:40:31,160
They're going to fall.

2010
00:40:31,160 --> 00:40:32,760
We have to do something about this.

2011
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:35,460
And Paul says, let God parent his children.

2012
00:40:35,460 --> 00:40:39,480
Let God do it.

2013
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:41,940
You're not going to make anybody stand or anybody.

2014
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:43,340
Well, you can make people fall.

2015
00:40:43,340 --> 00:40:47,100
But he says, look, the Lord will hold them up.

2016
00:40:47,100 --> 00:40:54,240
I only got one kid right now, but I imagine parenting multiple children is a bit more nuanced

2017
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:55,440
than parenting one child.

2018
00:40:55,440 --> 00:41:00,860
I imagine that if the Lord blesses me with a second child, that I am not going to parent

2019
00:41:00,860 --> 00:41:05,640
that child exactly the way that I parent Rory because they're two unique individuals with

2020
00:41:05,640 --> 00:41:09,280
unique backgrounds, with unique DNA, like, right?

2021
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:12,860
And Paul's saying here, let God parent his kids.

2022
00:41:12,860 --> 00:41:18,600
Don't break fellowship with your siblings because you think they should live like you

2023
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,720
and they think you should live like them.

2024
00:41:21,700 --> 00:41:26,820
It's actually so much better for the family of God that we live together in the midst of

2025
00:41:26,820 --> 00:41:28,940
difficult disagreements and unity.

2026
00:41:28,940 --> 00:41:30,540
We all grow.

2027
00:41:30,540 --> 00:41:33,540
We all conform to the image of Jesus as we learn from one another.

2028
00:41:33,540 --> 00:41:35,340
Make sense?

2029
00:41:35,340 --> 00:41:36,400
All right.

2030
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:37,040
Second principle.

2031
00:41:37,040 --> 00:41:39,380
I didn't even give you time to answer that.

2032
00:41:39,380 --> 00:41:41,200
I just assumed that it made sense, but we're going on.

2033
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:45,640
Number two, don't judge one another because God will judge you both.

2034
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:51,180
Now, it's important before we go on that I say we're talking about disputable matters.

2035
00:41:51,180 --> 00:41:56,960
There are times in which we are called to lovingly bring judgment to our brothers and sisters if

2036
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:58,860
they are living in open, unrepentant sin.

2037
00:41:58,860 --> 00:42:00,360
We're going to talk about that next week.

2038
00:42:00,360 --> 00:42:01,480
We don't have time for that this week.

2039
00:42:01,620 --> 00:42:06,120
So, disputable matters, do not judge one another because God will judge you both.

2040
00:42:06,120 --> 00:42:06,700
Verse 5.

2041
00:42:06,700 --> 00:42:11,480
One person that seems one day is better than another, while another seems all days alike.

2042
00:42:11,480 --> 00:42:14,500
Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind.

2043
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:16,060
Listen to this.

2044
00:42:16,060 --> 00:42:16,640
This is beautiful.

2045
00:42:16,640 --> 00:42:17,140
Paul says,

2046
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:37,700
Isn't that beautiful?

2047
00:42:39,000 --> 00:43:05,120
Paul's point in this section is that both groups believe what they believe and are doing

2048
00:43:05,120 --> 00:43:07,220
what they are doing in order to honor the Lord.

2049
00:43:07,220 --> 00:43:09,080
Their motivations are pure and right.

2050
00:43:09,080 --> 00:43:13,460
Both the weak and the strong are making the decisions they're making.

2051
00:43:13,460 --> 00:43:17,620
They're having the opinions that they have in order to honor God.

2052
00:43:17,620 --> 00:43:23,920
And both of them are going to stand before God one day and give an account for the decisions

2053
00:43:23,920 --> 00:43:24,700
that they made.

2054
00:43:24,700 --> 00:43:29,020
And both of them are probably going to be wrong on some of the decisions that they made.

2055
00:43:29,020 --> 00:43:36,680
And God, who is our loving Father and just judge, will work all of that out in the end.

2056
00:43:36,680 --> 00:43:38,660
It is not our job to figure that out here.

2057
00:43:38,660 --> 00:43:44,780
We're all going to be lovingly corrected by Jesus on disputable matters.

2058
00:43:44,780 --> 00:43:50,540
So let's spend time allowing him to search our hearts and reveal where we are getting things wrong.

2059
00:43:51,940 --> 00:43:56,780
The less time you spend correcting others, the more time you have to allow Jesus to correct you.

2060
00:43:56,780 --> 00:44:00,020
And the closer we will all get to the heart of the Father.

2061
00:44:00,020 --> 00:44:09,940
But I think one of the reasons we struggle with this is, I don't think any of you are like this.

2062
00:44:09,940 --> 00:44:10,440
It's just me.

2063
00:44:12,780 --> 00:44:20,500
I believe the best about my motivations, and I assume the worst about the motivations of those who are doing something different than me.

2064
00:44:22,880 --> 00:44:23,280
Thanks.

2065
00:44:23,280 --> 00:44:24,120
Appreciate that.

2066
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:25,620
Right?

2067
00:44:25,620 --> 00:44:29,800
It's like, no, I'm doing, I'm not doing the thing because my heart's in the right place.

2068
00:44:29,800 --> 00:44:33,760
So therefore, they must be doing the thing because their heart's in the wrong place.

2069
00:44:33,760 --> 00:44:35,840
And Paul here is very clear in this passage.

2070
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:38,380
Both of them have their hearts in the right place.

2071
00:44:38,940 --> 00:44:41,140
Both groups are doing what they're doing to honor God.

2072
00:44:41,140 --> 00:44:44,520
And we miss this over and over and over again.

2073
00:44:44,520 --> 00:44:50,100
All right.

2074
00:44:50,100 --> 00:44:50,820
I don't have time for that.

2075
00:44:50,820 --> 00:44:51,180
Okay.

2076
00:44:51,180 --> 00:44:59,040
So as we begin to kind of land the plane, you guys are going to be proud of me.

2077
00:44:59,040 --> 00:45:01,040
I withheld some things there.

2078
00:45:01,040 --> 00:45:02,500
All right.

2079
00:45:02,500 --> 00:45:03,300
I never do that.

2080
00:45:03,300 --> 00:45:04,040
I'm proud of myself.

2081
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:04,360
Okay.

2082
00:45:04,360 --> 00:45:04,780
Let's go.

2083
00:45:04,780 --> 00:45:05,460
Pound the back.

2084
00:45:05,460 --> 00:45:05,720
Okay.

2085
00:45:06,340 --> 00:45:14,540
As we begin to land the plane, I want to quickly share five lies that I believe the enemy uses to cause the church to divide over disputable matters.

2086
00:45:14,540 --> 00:45:18,580
And full disclosure, I stole this from another pastor, but it was too good not to share.

2087
00:45:18,580 --> 00:45:18,960
Okay.

2088
00:45:18,960 --> 00:45:23,700
Number one, we confuse unity with uniformity.

2089
00:45:23,700 --> 00:45:28,240
We confuse unity with uniformity.

2090
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:35,320
We want, in order for unity to happen, we want everybody to believe exactly what we believe, to make the same decisions about disputable matters that we make.

2091
00:45:36,900 --> 00:45:40,320
And we think, well, if they're different than us, then one of us has to be wrong.

2092
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:43,100
And this passage very clearly says, no, you can both be right.

2093
00:45:43,100 --> 00:45:48,780
You can both honor God in your convictions on matters of opinion.

2094
00:45:48,780 --> 00:45:52,540
And it's actually better that you live together in the same space.

2095
00:45:52,540 --> 00:45:56,360
You make each other better.

2096
00:45:57,020 --> 00:46:02,020
These arguments done in a respectful and helpful way make the body of Christ better.

2097
00:46:02,020 --> 00:46:09,580
Second, we bind others by our conscience.

2098
00:46:09,580 --> 00:46:15,500
We have heard from the Lord something that is clear for us to do or not do.

2099
00:46:15,500 --> 00:46:16,220
Right?

2100
00:46:16,220 --> 00:46:17,680
Let's go back to the politics thing.

2101
00:46:18,120 --> 00:46:26,880
Like, the worst thing that I could do as a weak brother when it comes to politics is tell everybody else they have to live by my conviction.

2102
00:46:26,880 --> 00:46:29,820
I can tell you why I had that conviction.

2103
00:46:29,820 --> 00:46:31,520
I can argue with you.

2104
00:46:31,580 --> 00:46:35,600
I can give you argumental points about why I have come to this conclusion.

2105
00:46:35,600 --> 00:46:42,660
But if I say, you have to do everything the way that I do it or else you're sinning, I'm making myself judge and juror.

2106
00:46:44,140 --> 00:46:46,400
And I'm eliminating God from the process.

2107
00:46:46,400 --> 00:46:50,840
Don't bind others by your conscience.

2108
00:46:50,840 --> 00:46:54,320
You work out your conscience with the Lord in prayer.

2109
00:46:54,320 --> 00:46:58,500
And you have conversations with your brothers and sisters who are coming to different conclusions.

2110
00:46:58,500 --> 00:47:06,040
And you fight for unity in the midst of deep conflict on disputable matters.

2111
00:47:06,040 --> 00:47:09,200
Third, our preferences become our prejudices.

2112
00:47:09,200 --> 00:47:11,740
This one hurts.

2113
00:47:14,140 --> 00:47:19,220
We often choose where we go to church far more based on our preferences than anything else.

2114
00:47:19,220 --> 00:47:21,120
But we don't even acknowledge them as preferences.

2115
00:47:21,120 --> 00:47:24,440
We acknowledge them as the right way to do things.

2116
00:47:24,440 --> 00:47:30,440
So much of what we do at church is preference-based.

2117
00:47:30,440 --> 00:47:35,060
And if we allow it to become our prejudice, if we look at other churches who do things differently than we do,

2118
00:47:35,060 --> 00:47:37,940
if we look at other Christians who do things differently than we do,

2119
00:47:37,940 --> 00:47:40,440
and we make our preferences our prejudices,

2120
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:44,020
we will end up despising people who God called us to sit at the same table.

2121
00:47:44,140 --> 00:47:47,940
And look, I have a heart, and this will not be easy,

2122
00:47:47,940 --> 00:47:49,980
and I don't even have a strategic plan for it.

2123
00:47:49,980 --> 00:47:52,180
I don't know that you can't have a strategic plan for it.

2124
00:47:52,180 --> 00:47:57,820
But I would love for our church to become more ethnically diverse in the future.

2125
00:47:57,820 --> 00:47:59,880
And if we're going to do that,

2126
00:47:59,880 --> 00:48:04,180
we better be sure we know what our preferences are.

2127
00:48:04,880 --> 00:48:10,440
And we better be willing to lay them down because so often churches attract the same type of person

2128
00:48:10,440 --> 00:48:13,620
because we build our ministry and our methodology around our preferences,

2129
00:48:13,620 --> 00:48:15,720
and we make our preferences our prejudices.

2130
00:48:15,720 --> 00:48:21,340
We've got to be willing to have an open hand about the type of songs we sing,

2131
00:48:21,340 --> 00:48:23,000
how often we sing the songs,

2132
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:24,220
what happens during worship,

2133
00:48:24,220 --> 00:48:25,520
what doesn't happen during worship,

2134
00:48:25,520 --> 00:48:26,460
all of these things.

2135
00:48:26,460 --> 00:48:28,800
If we're going to welcome a diverse group of people,

2136
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:31,180
we cannot make our preferences our prejudices.

2137
00:48:31,180 --> 00:48:34,500
Fourth, we seek to replace the ministry of the Holy Spirit.

2138
00:48:34,500 --> 00:48:38,680
Again, Paul says,

2139
00:48:38,680 --> 00:48:40,260
let God hold them up.

2140
00:48:40,260 --> 00:48:42,040
Let God deal with them.

2141
00:48:42,040 --> 00:48:44,980
You don't have to do his job for him.

2142
00:48:44,980 --> 00:48:50,240
See, we love the idea of doing God's job for him.

2143
00:48:50,300 --> 00:48:52,120
It's fun to, like, live it out,

2144
00:48:52,120 --> 00:48:55,860
but the responsibility is far too big for us to handle.

2145
00:48:55,860 --> 00:49:01,240
So, do not replace the Holy Spirit in somebody else's life.

2146
00:49:01,240 --> 00:49:05,920
Lastly, we prioritize winning an argument over winning a person.

2147
00:49:05,920 --> 00:49:10,760
We'd much rather just be right or convince ourselves that we're right

2148
00:49:10,760 --> 00:49:12,820
so we can sleep better at night

2149
00:49:12,820 --> 00:49:16,040
than winning a person,

2150
00:49:16,040 --> 00:49:17,960
which is the whole point of all of this.

2151
00:49:18,540 --> 00:49:19,560
People are the point.

2152
00:49:19,560 --> 00:49:21,960
Unity with one another is the point.

2153
00:49:21,960 --> 00:49:25,860
So, if we're going to have a church

2154
00:49:25,860 --> 00:49:28,760
that is successful at reaching a diverse group of people

2155
00:49:28,760 --> 00:49:30,700
and remains unified and effective,

2156
00:49:30,700 --> 00:49:33,360
we have to daily choose to accept one another

2157
00:49:33,360 --> 00:49:34,800
because God has accepted us

2158
00:49:34,800 --> 00:49:37,940
and not to judge one another over disputable matters

2159
00:49:37,940 --> 00:49:40,040
because God's going to judge all of us.

2160
00:49:40,040 --> 00:49:44,020
Don't hear me saying that you're not allowed to have opinions.

2161
00:49:44,020 --> 00:49:47,040
Lord knows I have opinions.

2162
00:49:47,760 --> 00:49:48,420
Lots of them.

2163
00:49:48,420 --> 00:49:49,640
Just come talk to me afterwards.

2164
00:49:49,640 --> 00:49:51,980
I will give you all of my opinions on all of the things.

2165
00:49:51,980 --> 00:49:54,200
Actually, I won't because I'm your pastor

2166
00:49:54,200 --> 00:49:56,440
and I don't want to cause you to stumble,

2167
00:49:56,440 --> 00:49:57,500
but I have them.

2168
00:49:57,500 --> 00:49:58,200
Believe me.

2169
00:49:58,200 --> 00:50:00,800
You can have your opinions,

2170
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:04,360
but make sure your opinions are rooted in prayerful study of God's word

2171
00:50:04,360 --> 00:50:07,020
and a willingness to listen and submit to the Holy Spirit.

2172
00:50:07,020 --> 00:50:09,940
So many Christians who think they're strong,

2173
00:50:10,940 --> 00:50:14,660
think they're strong on an opinion

2174
00:50:14,660 --> 00:50:16,000
or only strong on that opinion

2175
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:18,700
because they haven't even considered what God thinks about it.

2176
00:50:18,700 --> 00:50:21,380
They've just convinced themselves that they're good.

2177
00:50:21,380 --> 00:50:23,240
Of course I can do this.

2178
00:50:23,240 --> 00:50:24,880
Of course I can live this way.

2179
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:26,040
Of course I can act this way.

2180
00:50:28,600 --> 00:50:29,760
Same thing on the weak, right?

2181
00:50:29,760 --> 00:50:30,320
The weaks.

2182
00:50:30,320 --> 00:50:32,060
There are people on weak side

2183
00:50:32,060 --> 00:50:35,000
who literally have just accepted some man's rules.

2184
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:36,960
Some pastor told them,

2185
00:50:36,960 --> 00:50:38,060
here's the check boxes.

2186
00:50:38,060 --> 00:50:39,080
Here are the black and whites.

2187
00:50:39,080 --> 00:50:39,660
And you just say,

2188
00:50:39,660 --> 00:50:40,760
yeah, that's got to be right.

2189
00:50:42,660 --> 00:50:43,740
Whichever side you're on,

2190
00:50:43,740 --> 00:50:49,240
please make sure that your opinions are rooted in God's word.

2191
00:50:49,240 --> 00:50:52,120
Listening to the Holy Spirit.

2192
00:50:52,120 --> 00:50:54,180
God, is this what you would have for me to do?

2193
00:50:54,180 --> 00:50:56,220
Is this how you would have me to live?

2194
00:50:56,220 --> 00:50:59,000
And then once you form those opinions in that way,

2195
00:50:59,000 --> 00:51:01,880
bring them with an open hand

2196
00:51:01,880 --> 00:51:04,500
to a brother or sister who doesn't agree with you.

2197
00:51:04,500 --> 00:51:07,420
Have a beneficial conversation.

2198
00:51:07,420 --> 00:51:10,300
Have a meaningful conversation with a brother or sister

2199
00:51:10,300 --> 00:51:13,200
who disagrees with you on a disputable issue

2200
00:51:13,200 --> 00:51:14,700
and do so with honor.

2201
00:51:14,700 --> 00:51:20,260
And you might just find that God uses you

2202
00:51:20,260 --> 00:51:21,100
to change their mind.

2203
00:51:21,100 --> 00:51:25,460
Or God forbid he might use them to change your mind.

2204
00:51:25,460 --> 00:51:29,000
But the worst case scenario

2205
00:51:29,000 --> 00:51:31,560
in that hypothetical

2206
00:51:31,560 --> 00:51:34,500
is you both walk away loving God

2207
00:51:34,500 --> 00:51:35,560
and loving each other more

2208
00:51:35,560 --> 00:51:36,660
in the midst of your disagreement.

2209
00:51:36,660 --> 00:51:39,960
And that, my friends,

2210
00:51:39,960 --> 00:51:41,520
is Paul's entire point.

2211
00:51:41,520 --> 00:51:43,200
Chapter 14 and 15.

2212
00:51:43,200 --> 00:51:43,880
He wraps up,

2213
00:51:43,880 --> 00:51:45,880
we didn't go through the whole text,

2214
00:51:45,880 --> 00:51:46,980
but he wraps up his argument.

2215
00:51:46,980 --> 00:51:48,100
He starts it in 14.1

2216
00:51:48,100 --> 00:51:49,740
and he finishes it in 15.7,

2217
00:51:49,740 --> 00:51:50,480
which he says,

2218
00:51:50,480 --> 00:51:53,140
therefore, welcome one another

2219
00:51:53,140 --> 00:51:54,920
as Christ has welcomed you

2220
00:51:54,920 --> 00:51:56,460
for the glory of God.

2221
00:51:56,460 --> 00:51:59,980
This is the point.

2222
00:51:59,980 --> 00:52:04,620
We'd sit around the same table

2223
00:52:04,620 --> 00:52:07,220
looking to Jesus at the head,

2224
00:52:08,200 --> 00:52:09,220
looking to one another

2225
00:52:09,220 --> 00:52:10,820
in the midst of our disagreements.

2226
00:52:10,820 --> 00:52:13,640
Disunity grieves the heart of God

2227
00:52:13,640 --> 00:52:14,860
and it renders the church

2228
00:52:14,860 --> 00:52:16,220
ineffective of our mission.

2229
00:52:16,220 --> 00:52:21,740
May we prioritize unity

2230
00:52:21,740 --> 00:52:22,820
in the midst of diversity.

2231
00:52:22,820 --> 00:52:25,420
May we have our opinions

2232
00:52:25,420 --> 00:52:26,520
in open hands.

2233
00:52:30,520 --> 00:52:31,300
I think we're,

2234
00:52:31,300 --> 00:52:35,120
pastoral, I'll just say,

2235
00:52:35,120 --> 00:52:36,440
I think we're relatively okay

2236
00:52:36,440 --> 00:52:37,420
at this here,

2237
00:52:37,420 --> 00:52:40,420
but man, may we not lose sight of it.

2238
00:52:40,420 --> 00:52:43,840
And may we not have blind spots

2239
00:52:43,840 --> 00:52:45,600
or think, get comfortable with this.

2240
00:52:45,600 --> 00:52:49,600
If you're in here

2241
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:50,900
and you're not a follower of Jesus,

2242
00:52:52,120 --> 00:52:54,780
I hope that what you heard today

2243
00:52:54,780 --> 00:52:56,780
was that God designed his church

2244
00:52:56,780 --> 00:52:57,900
to be the most welcoming,

2245
00:52:57,900 --> 00:53:00,180
diverse, and unified place on earth.

2246
00:53:00,180 --> 00:53:03,120
And we have not lived up

2247
00:53:03,120 --> 00:53:04,020
to our end of the bargain.

2248
00:53:04,020 --> 00:53:08,280
Don't hold that against him.

2249
00:53:10,980 --> 00:53:12,200
See so many people

2250
00:53:12,200 --> 00:53:14,420
who refuse to even consider

2251
00:53:14,420 --> 00:53:15,760
the claims of Jesus

2252
00:53:15,760 --> 00:53:18,640
because of the failures of the church.

2253
00:53:18,640 --> 00:53:20,200
If you're in here

2254
00:53:20,200 --> 00:53:21,080
and if you're struggling

2255
00:53:21,080 --> 00:53:21,800
with Christianity

2256
00:53:21,800 --> 00:53:23,040
because you see the way

2257
00:53:23,040 --> 00:53:24,600
Christians living out the faith,

2258
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:27,320
do not hold our actions against him.

2259
00:53:27,320 --> 00:53:28,680
Consider his words.

2260
00:53:28,680 --> 00:53:30,720
Consider his invitation

2261
00:53:30,720 --> 00:53:34,040
to be welcomed to this family,

2262
00:53:34,040 --> 00:53:36,580
diverse and unified people.

2263
00:53:36,580 --> 00:53:39,820
Submit to him as Lord.

2264
00:53:39,820 --> 00:53:41,340
Bring your strengths

2265
00:53:41,340 --> 00:53:42,220
into our community

2266
00:53:42,220 --> 00:53:43,480
and help us live out

2267
00:53:43,480 --> 00:53:45,780
his desire for his church.

2268
00:53:45,780 --> 00:53:50,840
Welcome one another

2269
00:53:50,840 --> 00:53:53,260
as Christ has welcomed you

2270
00:53:53,260 --> 00:53:55,540
for the glory of God.

2271
00:53:55,540 --> 00:53:57,540
Let's pray.

2272
00:54:00,720 --> 00:54:07,360
Father,

2273
00:54:07,360 --> 00:54:09,780
we are so grateful

2274
00:54:09,780 --> 00:54:12,340
that you have set a table

2275
00:54:12,340 --> 00:54:14,840
in the presence of our enemies.

2276
00:54:14,840 --> 00:54:18,100
That you sit at the head

2277
00:54:18,100 --> 00:54:18,720
of that table

2278
00:54:18,720 --> 00:54:19,800
and you invite

2279
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:21,700
male and female,

2280
00:54:21,700 --> 00:54:22,860
slave and free,

2281
00:54:22,860 --> 00:54:24,160
Jew and Gentile,

2282
00:54:24,160 --> 00:54:25,520
Democrat and Republican.

2283
00:54:30,720 --> 00:54:32,900
You invite a diverse group

2284
00:54:32,900 --> 00:54:33,340
of people

2285
00:54:33,340 --> 00:54:34,340
from a diverse group

2286
00:54:34,340 --> 00:54:34,920
of backgrounds

2287
00:54:34,920 --> 00:54:37,080
all on the one,

2288
00:54:37,080 --> 00:54:39,740
on the singular basis

2289
00:54:39,740 --> 00:54:40,460
that we're willing

2290
00:54:40,460 --> 00:54:41,480
to bow our knee

2291
00:54:41,480 --> 00:54:42,340
to you as Lord.

2292
00:54:42,340 --> 00:54:45,020
And if we're really willing

2293
00:54:45,020 --> 00:54:45,520
to do that,

2294
00:54:45,520 --> 00:54:46,160
everything else

2295
00:54:46,160 --> 00:54:47,140
will take care of itself.

2296
00:54:47,140 --> 00:54:51,200
God, may we be a people

2297
00:54:51,200 --> 00:54:53,380
who come to that table

2298
00:54:53,380 --> 00:54:56,380
laying down our opinions,

2299
00:54:56,380 --> 00:54:57,780
our preferences,

2300
00:54:59,520 --> 00:55:00,560
bowing our knee

2301
00:55:00,560 --> 00:55:02,320
to Jesus as Lord

2302
00:55:02,320 --> 00:55:06,740
whose rules

2303
00:55:06,740 --> 00:55:07,520
and regulations

2304
00:55:07,520 --> 00:55:08,740
are love the Lord your God

2305
00:55:08,740 --> 00:55:09,460
with all of your heart,

2306
00:55:09,460 --> 00:55:10,420
soul, mind, and strength

2307
00:55:10,420 --> 00:55:11,060
and love your neighbor

2308
00:55:11,060 --> 00:55:11,620
as yourself.

2309
00:55:11,620 --> 00:55:12,700
God, if we do that well,

2310
00:55:12,700 --> 00:55:15,940
I know that unity will happen.

2311
00:55:15,940 --> 00:55:19,120
God, may we be a diverse

2312
00:55:19,120 --> 00:55:20,360
and unified body

2313
00:55:20,360 --> 00:55:23,580
that the world around us

2314
00:55:23,580 --> 00:55:25,980
looks in and sees

2315
00:55:25,980 --> 00:55:28,000
and says something is different

2316
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:29,360
about those people.

2317
00:55:29,360 --> 00:55:30,400
They're able to have

2318
00:55:30,400 --> 00:55:31,440
hard conversations

2319
00:55:31,440 --> 00:55:32,580
with dignity

2320
00:55:32,580 --> 00:55:33,680
and with respect.

2321
00:55:33,680 --> 00:55:35,120
They're able to lock arms

2322
00:55:35,120 --> 00:55:36,400
with brothers and sisters

2323
00:55:36,400 --> 00:55:37,440
who don't look like them,

2324
00:55:37,440 --> 00:55:38,140
talk like them,

2325
00:55:38,140 --> 00:55:38,840
vote like them,

2326
00:55:38,840 --> 00:55:40,200
believe certain things

2327
00:55:40,200 --> 00:55:41,200
that they believe.

2328
00:55:41,200 --> 00:55:44,920
And yet,

2329
00:55:44,920 --> 00:55:47,960
they find unity

2330
00:55:47,960 --> 00:55:48,820
because of their love

2331
00:55:48,820 --> 00:55:50,060
for this Jesus.

2332
00:55:50,220 --> 00:55:51,860
God, may we be an effective,

2333
00:55:51,860 --> 00:55:53,800
unified church

2334
00:55:53,800 --> 00:55:54,540
for your glory.

2335
00:55:54,540 --> 00:55:57,160
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

2336
00:55:57,160 --> 00:55:58,060
Amen.
